Justification

A lot of Information Technology jobs or hobbies are usually acted out at home, and though there are times you are at an educational institute, those who are either graduated or self-taught usually don’t have immediate access to help. 

Instead of interrupting work by using a phone or keyboard, risking becoming distracted by social media or distractions – the Pocket Professor provides hands-free guidance, allowing the user to remain focused on their task while receiving direction via hints.

Project Deliverables

The Pocket Professor deliverable is a physical model of a miniature Information Technology Professor, capable of observing a user’s workspace and providing hints in response to IT-related questions.

Intermediate Deliverables
Functional Prototype
The Pocket Professor can power on and off
Camera functionality is responsive and operational
Physical Reaction or feedback are demonstrated 
(E.G: reacting when being placed face-down)

Integrated Learning Response System
Pocket Professor provides only hints and not full answers to questions
Responses are consistent and appropriate based on user input

Final Deliverable
Fully assembled Pocket Professor Model 
(Rough Draft shown in Figures 01 & 02)
Ability to accept user questions and provide hint-based responses
Functional live-camera
