Acceptance Criteria

Acceptance of the Pocket Professor deliverables will be based on successful demonstration of the following criteria:

The Pocket Professors turns on and off reliably
When the Pocket Professor is laying face-down, it will react and say something along the lines of “Help me” or complain
The Pocket Professor responds when asked a question relating to IT
The Pocket Professor can stand upright on its own (without external support)
Responses are appropriate and relevant
Responds to questions with hints within 5 seconds
Scope
Inclusions
The following are within the Scope for this project:

Physical 8-inch model of a professor
Raspberry Pi with open-source AI integration
Live camera for visual assessment
Voice input (hands-free questions)
Voice output (hint-based responses)
Orientation detection (face-down reaction)
Ability to stand independently
IT-focused hint responses (not full answers)

Exclusions
The following are OUT OF SCOPE for this project:

Mobile app or web interface for remote access to the Pocket Professor
Support for non-english languages
Physical animations 
Voice Training

Assumptions
Users ask primarily IT-related questions
Open-source models suitable for IT knowledge exist and are available
Voice interaction is primary (may include text fallback)
Physical reactions don't require complex mechanics
Team has basic electronics and Python experience


Constraints
Budget: Limited to available/affordable components
Hardware: Must run on Raspberry Pi (limited processing power)
Size: 8-10 inches tall (pocket-sized)
Power: Battery or AC powered with reasonable runtime
AI: Open-source models only
Timeline: Around 10 weeks
